Emacs Reader (also EmacsReader and emacs-reader) is a document reader
for [[GNU Emacs]], which supports many different document formats by
making use of [https://mupdf.com/ the MuPDF library].

Emacs Reader only relies on !MuPDF, and not on DocViewMode,
[[PDFTools]], or <code>nov.el</code>; as it seeks to be a better
replacement for all of those, particularly with better performance for
browsing large PDFs.

== Supported formats ==

Formats with first-class support include:

* CBZ comic book archives,
* [[EPUB]] e‑books,
* FB2 !FictionBook e‑books,
* Mobipocket (<code>.prc,</code> and <code>.mobi</code>) e‑books,
* !OpenXPS, also known as XPS – the Open XML Paper Specification, and
* [[PDF]].

Other formats, such as OpenDocument formats can be viewed, but cannot
then be edited in Emacs, you're better off using e. g. !LibreOffice
instead.  Similarly, Microsoft Office formats have some limited
support for viewing in !MuPDF, but again, not editing.

== Installing Emacs Reader ==

Currently (September 2026), Emacs Reader is not (yet) in any [[ELPA]],
so you have clone the git repo to install it,
[https://codeberg.org/MonadicSheep/emacs-reader#user-content-outline-container-headline-8
see instructions in Emacs Reader’s README].

